# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
#
# GlintfxPkgConfigValidateInstalled.cmake.in - PKG-VALIDATE.
#
# Configured with configure_file(@ONLY) by
# glintfx_register_pkgconfig_validation() (cmake/GlintfxPkgConfigValidate.cmake)
# into <build>/GlintfxPkgConfigValidateInstalled.cmake, then
# include()-d from ONE install(CODE) line appended right after
# glintfx.pc's own install(FILES ...) (glintfx_install_pkgconfig(),
# cmake/GlintfxInstall.cmake). By the time this file runs, glintfx.pc,
# the public headers and the library artifact are already on disk, in
# whatever real layout THIS `cmake --install` invocation actually
# produced, on the machine actually running it - a packager we have
# never met, using a layout tests/tools/check_pkgconfig.sh (PKG-DIST)
# never enumerated, because PKG-DIST's six scenarios only prove what
# OUR OWN CI exercises (GODS_LAWS.md LEI ZERO: the base of consumers
# is public and unknown, so a validator that only runs in our CI
# leaves every layout outside it unchecked, silently).
#
# HOW THIS FILE LOCATES THE INSTALL, WITHOUT PREDICTING IT (adversarial
# review round 3's ruling on check_pkgconfig.sh, relayed verbatim in
# that file's own header: "parar de prever a entrada e passar a
# validar a saida" - the same ruling applies here, one layer earlier):
# @GLINTFX_NORMALIZED_INSTALL_LIBDIR@ below is the ONLY thing baked in
# by configure_file(@ONLY) - a plain, already-normalized string read
# from this build's own CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR
# (glintfx_register_pkgconfig_validation(), which computes it with the
# exact same cmake_path(NORMAL_PATH) call
# glintfx_compute_pkgconfig_relocatable_prefix() in
# cmake/GlintfxInstall.cmake already uses for glintfx.pc's own
# content), because that value cannot change between configure and
# install - it is a CACHE variable, fixed once. Both
# "${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}" and "$ENV{DESTDIR}" below stay LITERAL,
# unsubstituted text in THIS FILE: configure_file(@ONLY) only ever
# replaces @VAR@ forms, never ${VAR} or $ENV{VAR} - the exact escaping
# technique glintfx_compute_pkgconfig_relocatable_prefix() already
# uses for glintfx.pc's own "${pcfiledir}". That is what lets them
# resolve to the REAL, INSTALL-TIME values when this file actually
# runs: CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX reflects any `cmake --install --prefix
# <p>` override (cmake_install.cmake pre-defines it before any
# install(CODE) block runs - confirmed against a real generated
# cmake_install.cmake on this machine), and $ENV{DESTDIR} is read
# fresh from the environment of THIS invocation - the staging root
# that, per PACKAGING.md, "does not exist, and is not knowable, at
# CMake CONFIGURE time".
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT TRY TO HANDLE, DECLARED (GODS_LAWS.md L-27,
# honest downgrade over silent overclaiming):
#   - Cross-compilation needs nothing special here: every check below
#     either reads the filesystem/glintfx.pc's own text directly (no
#     binary involved at all - the content check, see "Talking to the
#     pkg-config BINARY itself" below) or runs `pkg-config`/`pkgconf`,
#     a HOST tool operating on text (the one binary-conversation
#     check) - neither ever executes the target-arch library or an
#     object file, so nothing here is target-arch sensitive.
#   - Component-scoped installs (`cmake --install --component X`)
#     need nothing special either, and this is a property of THIS
#     PROJECT today, not a general claim: none of glintfx's install()
#     rules (library, headers, CMake package, glintfx.pc, and this
#     validation's own install(CODE)) declare a COMPONENT, so they all
#     share the implicit default component - CMake's generated
#     cmake_install.cmake wraps every one of them, this file's
#     include() line included, in the identical
#     `if(NOT CMAKE_INSTALL_COMPONENT OR CMAKE_INSTALL_COMPONENT
#     STREQUAL "Unspecified")` guard (confirmed against a real
#     generated cmake_install.cmake on this machine). A
#     `--component <name>` install for any OTHER name installs
#     NOTHING for this project at all - no library, no headers, no
#     glintfx.pc - and this validation is skipped right along with
#     them, for the same reason, not by any special-casing here. If a
#     future fatia splits glintfx's install() rules into distinct
#     COMPONENTs, this file's own install(CODE) registration
#     (glintfx_register_pkgconfig_validation(), cmake/GlintfxPkgConfigValidate.cmake)
#     needs a COMPONENT argument added at the same time, or it would
#     start running against a partial, intentionally-incomplete
#     component install and misreport that as broken.
#   - What "Libs.private carries the right linker token for a static
#     build" MEANS (its content, and that it is genuinely load-bearing
#     for a real static link) is PKG-DIST's own, already-tested claim
#     (tests/tools/check_pkgconfig.sh's static scenario). This file
#     only proves every PATH glintfx.pc emits (via a plain,
#     non-`--static` `--cflags`/`--libs` query - the one every
#     consumer hits) resolves to something real; re-querying
#     `--static` here would duplicate a claim already covered
#     elsewhere without covering any layout PKG-DIST's own scenario 5
#     does not already reach.
#   - Windows library-artifact naming: RESOLVED, not out of scope
#     (PKG-WIN-SCOPE, revertido por ordem do lider, 27/08/2026). An
#     earlier fatia (decisao do CTO, ja assinada) had wrapped BOTH
#     glintfx_install_pkgconfig() and
#     glintfx_register_pkgconfig_validation() in if(UNIX) in
#     CMakeLists.txt specifically because this file's library-artifact
#     glob only ever matched libglintfx.so*/libglintfx.a and would
#     have reported a false failure against glintfx.lib. The lider
#     derrubou essa decisao: the if(UNIX) guard in CMakeLists.txt is
#     gone, both calls run on every platform again, and the glob below
#     (glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_variable() and
#     glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_flags()) now matches glintfx.lib too -
#     the archive artifact CMakeLists.txt's OUTPUT_NAME/ARCHIVE
#     DESTINATION rule (cmake/GlintfxLibrary.cmake,
#     cmake/GlintfxInstall.cmake) actually produces there, for both a
#     shared build's import library and a static build's archive (MSVC
#     uses the same .lib extension for both).
#   - Talking to the pkg-config BINARY itself, as opposed to reading
#     the filesystem, is where this file draws its one platform-shaped
#     line (glintfx_validate_installed_pkgconfig() below) - and, since
#     PKG-WIN-SCOPE's adversarial review round 4 (27/08/2026), that
#     line is drawn by CONSTRUCTION, not by hoping the order of two
#     unrelated things never crosses: every filesystem-only check -
#     glintfx.pc exists, the staged pkgconfig/ directory exists, the
#     library/header artifacts are on disk, and every -I/-L token a
#     plain (non-`--static`) Cflags:/Libs: line would emit resolves to
#     real, populated content - reads glintfx.pc's OWN text and
#     resolves its "${var}"/"${pcfiledir}" substitutions itself
#     (glintfx_pkgconfig_read_raw_variables(),
#     glintfx_pkgconfig_resolve_variables(),
#     glintfx_pkgconfig_substitute_text() below), calls NO pkg-config
#     binary at all, and runs UNCONDITIONALLY, before this file ever
#     tries to find or talk to one - on every platform, Windows
#     included, with FATAL_ERROR veto power that never downgrades.
#     ACHADO (adversarial review, 27/08/2026, reproduced live before
#     this fix): the PREVIOUS shape of this file ran those same
#     checks only AFTER a successful `pkg-config --exists` binary
#     call, so on Windows, when that ONE binary call failed for any
#     reason at all - including one that has nothing to do with
#     whether the library artifact is genuinely on disk - the WARNING
#     branch below fired having never looked at the filesystem, and
#     still told the packager "Filesystem-based checks already
#     confirmed ... the library artifact ... genuinely on disk". A
#     real install with ONLY the compiled library artifact deleted,
#     re-validated with WIN32 forced, printed exactly that sentence at
#     exit 0. The fix is this file's own structure now: the
#     filesystem/text-only content check runs first and never depends
#     on whether any pkg-config binary can even be found, so nothing
#     downstream of it can ever again claim a veto it did not
#     exercise.
#
#     What DOES still talk to a real pkg-config binary, and is
#     therefore still the one platform-shaped line: confirming that a
#     REAL pkg-config on THIS machine's PATH also finds glintfx via
#     `--exists` (PKG_CONFIG_PATH resolution, .pc syntax parsing by an
#     implementation this project does not control) - a genuinely
#     different claim than "the content glintfx.pc describes is
#     really on disk", and the only one that can plausibly vary by
#     which pkg-config a packager happens to have. On GitHub Actions'
#     windows-latest runner, the only pkg-config on PATH is Strawberry
#     Perl's Pure-Perl `PkgConfig` reimplementation (`pkg-config.bat`),
#     which - MEASURED against a live fixture by
#     tools/ci/diagnose-win-pkgconfig.ps1, GHA run 33050708122, job
#     "Windows - compartilhado" - resolves a bare PKG_CONFIG_PATH
#     value shaped like "C:/Users/.../pkgconfig" (no explicit list
#     separator) by falling back to POSIX-style splitting on ':',
#     which shreds the drive letter itself ("C:") into a bogus
#     one-letter search directory; the SAME value with an explicit
#     trailing ';' resolves correctly, because the presence of ';'
#     makes it split on the Windows-native separator instead. That
#     measured, real fix - append a native list separator before
#     talking to pkg-config on Windows - is applied below. It is not
#     provable in general, for every pkg-config a packager on some
#     other Windows machine might have on PATH (a real MSYS2 pkgconf,
#     a vcpkg-shipped one, or anything else GODS_LAWS.md LEI ZERO's
#     public-and-unknown consumer base might combine with Windows) -
#     so if the conversation with the binary still fails after this
#     fix, glintfx_validate_installed_pkgconfig() reports it as a
#     WARNING on Windows, not a FATAL_ERROR, and - now honestly -
#     names ONLY that one conversation as unverified: the
#     filesystem/text-only content check above it already ran, on
#     THIS same invocation, and already had full veto power over
#     whatever it found. On every Unix target this project tests, the
#     veto stays exactly as strict as it always was - no downgrade
#     there, and none of it was ever binary-dependent in the first
#     place.
#
#   - PKG-WIN-SCOPE, adversarial review round 5 (27/08/2026) - CRITICAL,
#     reproduced live, in the OTHER direction from every finding above:
#     a genuinely BROKEN install passing as verified, not a genuinely
#     good one being rejected. glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_variable()
#     and glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_flags() below used to
#     resolve every relative includedir/libdir/-I/-L value with
#     cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH ...) and no BASE_DIRECTORY, which in
#     CMake script mode (exactly how this file always runs) resolves
#     against the CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY of whoever invoked
#     `cmake --install`/`cmake -P` - the DISPATCH directory, not
#     anything this file controls. MEASURED attack: a real install with
#     its compiled library artifact deleted, a glintfx.pc edited to a
#     relative libdir, and the validator invoked from an unrelated
#     directory that happened to contain a decoy file matching the same
#     glob pattern - PASSED at EXIT=0, "validation passed", about an
#     install whose actual library had just been deleted. This is the
#     exact "confirmado no disco" claim this entire validator exists to
#     make, defeated by nothing more than the caller's own CWD. Fixed
#     by anchoring every relative resolution to "pcfiledir" instead -
#     glintfx.pc's OWN parent directory, read from this function's
#     already-absolute pc_file argument via cmake_path(GET ... PARENT_PATH),
#     never predicted and never influenced by where the command was
#     run from. Three call sites, all fixed the same way (see each
#     function's own comment below for the reasoning specific to it):
#     glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_variable()'s "value",
#     glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_flags()'s "-I" and "-L" token
#     resolution. At the time of round 5, confirmed this was the ONLY
#     place in this file (and, searched, the only place in glintfx's
#     whole cmake/ tree) that called cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH ...)
#     without an explicit BASE_DIRECTORY. Round 6 below (27/08/2026)
#     adds a second, DELIBERATE one - a different question entirely
#     (where CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX itself physically resolves on disk),
#     with a different, still-correct default (CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR
#     - the invoking CWD - not pcfiledir); see round 6's own comment
#     below for why that is not a repeat of this same finding.
#
#   - PKG-WIN-SCOPE, adversarial review round 5 (27/08/2026), same pass -
#     three SEPARATE defects in glintfx_pkgconfig_read_raw_variables()
#     below, all in the OPPOSITE direction (rejecting a genuinely GOOD
#     install), each measured against a real pkgconf 2.5.1 on this
#     machine rather than reasoned about: whitespace allowed around "="
#     in a variable assignment, a trailing "#..." comment on a variable
#     line, and a variable defined twice resolving to its LAST
#     definition rather than its first. See that function's own comment
#     for the measured detail on each; PACKAGING.md's own promise that
#     this validator resolves glintfx.pc "the same way a real pkg-config
#     would" was false for all three cases until this fix, and is
#     re-checked, phrase by phrase, against this fatia's own fix.
#
#   - PKG-WIN-SCOPE, adversarial review round 6 (27/08/2026) - CRITICAL
#     REGRESSION, introduced by round 5's own fix above, reproduced
#     live: an ORDINARY relative install prefix - `cmake --install
#     <build> --prefix ./stage`, nothing exotic, the shape any
#     packaging tutorial or CI script reaches for routinely - made a
#     genuinely GOOD install FAIL. MEASURED: `cd <a-dir> && cmake
#     --install <build> --prefix ./stage`, every file genuinely on
#     disk, printed "glintfx.pc's includedir resolves to
#     'stage/lib64/pkgconfig/stage/include', which does not exist on
#     disk", exit 1 - the DOUBLED "stage" names the defect precisely.
#     Round 5's own search does not find this one, because it hunted by
#     the SHAPE of a known bug (every call site of ONE specific
#     operation, cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH ... value/token ...) with no
#     BASE_DIRECTORY) rather than by enumerating every place a path gets
#     built, joined, or checked for existence - and this defect is one
#     layer EARLIER, in a DIFFERENT operation round 5 never looked at:
#     glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_resolve_staged_dir() above, in its
#     relative-CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR branch, built the staged pkgconfig/
#     directory as "${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/${libdir}/pkgconfig" via
#     cmake_path(APPEND ...), with CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX read RAW - never
#     forced absolute. `cmake --install` itself does not reject a
#     relative --prefix; it resolves it against the INVOKING PROCESS'S
#     CWD for the real, physical install (confirmed live, the SAME run
#     that then failed printed "-- Installing: <cwd>/./stage/lib64/...").
#     So when a packager passes one, this function's own
#     _glintfx_pkgconfig_dir stayed a RELATIVE string
#     ("stage/lib64/pkgconfig"). That string became pc_file, then
#     pc_file's own PARENT_PATH - glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_on_disk()'s
#     "pcfiledir" seed (line ~690), STILL relative - got substituted
#     LITERALLY into glintfx.pc's own "${pcfiledir}/../../include" text
#     by glintfx_pkgconfig_substitute_text() (plain text replacement, by
#     design, mirroring real pkg-config - it has no notion of "this one
#     happens to already be absolute"), producing a "value" that itself
#     STARTS WITH "stage/..." and therefore still reads as relative.
#     Round 5's own fix - correct, and left untouched here - then
#     anchors that relative "value" to "pcfiledir" via
#     cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH value BASE_DIRECTORY
#     "${_glintfx_content_variable_base_dir}" NORMALIZE), where the base
#     directory is computed from this SAME relative pc_file
#     (glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_variable()'s own PARENT_PATH,
#     line ~502): a relative base directory got a relative value
#     APPENDED onto it, and the shared "stage/lib64/pkgconfig" segment
#     landed in the result TWICE. Every downstream check was reading
#     real content that genuinely existed; nothing about the install
#     itself was ever broken.
#
#     THE FIX: glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_resolve_staged_dir()'s
#     relative-CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR branch now forces its own
#     CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX-derived variable absolute first, with
#     cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH ... NORMALIZE) and DELIBERATELY NO
#     explicit BASE_DIRECTORY - the exact shape the comment above (round
#     5) warns caused THAT bug. This is not a contradiction, because the
#     two calls answer two different questions. Round 5's sites resolve
#     a PKG-CONFIG-FILE-RELATIVE reference (includedir=, libdir=, an
#     -I/-L token), which must anchor to glintfx.pc's OWN directory
#     (pcfiledir) - pkg-config's own convention - never to the caller's
#     CWD; omitting BASE_DIRECTORY there was wrong for exactly that
#     reason. This site resolves CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX itself, answering
#     "where did `cmake --install`'s relative --prefix ACTUALLY write
#     files" - and CMake's own default BASE_DIRECTORY,
#     CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR (confirmed equal to the invoking
#     process's CWD in script mode, round 5's own finding above),
#     answers that correctly BY CONSTRUCTION, because it is the SAME
#     rule the real `cmake --install` used to decide where to physically
#     write those files in the first place (measured live: the "--
#     Installing: <cwd>/./stage/..." line above). Two different
#     questions, two different correct defaults.
#
#     Once _glintfx_pkgconfig_dir - and therefore pc_file, and therefore
#     every pcfiledir-seeded substitution and both validate_content_*
#     functions' own base directories - is absolute from this single
#     point on, every site round 5 already anchored to pcfiledir
#     resolves correctly with no further change needed there: an
#     already-absolute "value"/token short-circuits
#     cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH ...)'s own BASE_DIRECTORY entirely (it
#     only ever applies to a genuinely relative path), so the doubling
#     cannot recur through that mechanism either. tests/tools/
#     check_pkgconfig_validate.sh's own scenario 14 (relative --prefix,
#     dispatched from a throwaway directory, mutated back to reproduce
#     this exact regression) is the regression proof.
#
# Two escape hatches, both named GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION on
# purpose (one name, two mechanisms, same intent): the CACHE option in
# cmake/GlintfxOptions.cmake, read at CONFIGURE time by
# glintfx_register_pkgconfig_validation() BEFORE this file is even
# generated (skips it for good, for this build directory); and the
# ENVIRONMENT variable read at the top of
# glintfx_validate_installed_pkgconfig() below, at INSTALL time -
# because a packaging pipeline that configures ONCE and installs
# SEVERAL times against different DESTDIR/--component values (a real
# pattern: RPM's `%install` section can invoke `%cmake_install` more
# than once) should not have to reconfigure the whole tree just to
# skip this one check on one of those invocations.
#
# Each function below does one thing (GODS_LAWS.md L-17).

# Resolves the STAGED (DESTDIR-aware) pkgconfig/ directory this
# install actually wrote glintfx.pc into - never a predicted value,
# only the same inputs GNUInstallDirs' own install() rules already
# used to decide where to write it for real.
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_resolve_staged_dir out_var)
    cmake_path(SET _glintfx_configured_libdir NORMALIZE "@GLINTFX_NORMALIZED_INSTALL_LIBDIR@")

    if(IS_ABSOLUTE "${_glintfx_configured_libdir}")
        # GNUInstallDirs allows CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR to be absolute
        # (a packager staging into a fixed system location outside
        # CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX) - install() ignores CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX
        # entirely for an already-absolute DESTINATION, so this branch
        # must too (same rule glintfx_compute_pkgconfig_relocatable_prefix()
        # in cmake/GlintfxInstall.cmake already applies to glintfx.pc's
        # OWN prefix= content).
        set(_glintfx_dir_no_destdir "${_glintfx_configured_libdir}/pkgconfig")
    else()
        # PKG-WIN-SCOPE round 6 (27/08/2026): CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX is
        # forced absolute HERE, before anything is appended to it - see
        # this file's own header for the regression this closes and why
        # omitting BASE_DIRECTORY is the deliberately correct choice at
        # this one call site (it must match `cmake --install`'s own
        # resolution of a relative --prefix against the invoking
        # process's CWD, not glintfx.pc's pcfiledir). Read raw and left
        # relative, this used to make _glintfx_dir_no_destdir below - and
        # therefore pc_file, and therefore every pcfiledir-seeded
        # substitution downstream - relative too, which is what let a
        # relative "${pcfiledir}/../../include" substitution and a
        # relative BASE_DIRECTORY double up on the same "stage/..."
        # segment in glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_variable().
        set(_glintfx_prefix "${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}")
        cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH _glintfx_prefix NORMALIZE)
        cmake_path(APPEND _glintfx_prefix "${_glintfx_configured_libdir}" "pkgconfig"
            OUTPUT_VARIABLE _glintfx_dir_no_destdir)
    endif()

    if(DEFINED ENV{DESTDIR} AND NOT "$ENV{DESTDIR}" STREQUAL "")
        # DESTDIR is a plain, unconditional string PREFIX applied to
        # an already-absolute destination - deliberately NOT
        # cmake_path(APPEND), which treats an absolute right-hand
        # side as "replace the base", the opposite of what DESTDIR
        # means. This mirrors what CMake's own file(INSTALL) does
        # internally for the SAME reason (PACKAGING.md: "DESTDIR
        # prepends to EVERY destination, relative or absolute,
        # without changing any path baked into the installed files'
        # own content").
        set(${out_var} "$ENV{DESTDIR}${_glintfx_dir_no_destdir}" PARENT_SCOPE)
    else()
        set(${out_var} "${_glintfx_dir_no_destdir}" PARENT_SCOPE)
    endif()
endfunction()

# Filesystem patterns that name glintfx's own compiled library
# artifact, one glob per platform-shaped naming convention it is known
# to produce (cmake/GlintfxLibrary.cmake's OUTPUT_NAME "glintfx" is
# the same string on every platform; only the prefix/suffix a linker
# actually writes to disk differ). Both callers below
# (glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_variable's "library" content kind,
# and glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_flags' own -L check) call this instead of
# each keeping their own copy of the pattern list - PKG-WIN-SCOPE's
# first pass at Windows support (before the lider revertida it) had to
# extend two separate globs by hand and only remembered one; a single
# source of truth removes that failure mode (GODS_LAWS.md L-17).
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_library_glob_patterns out_var)
    set(${out_var}
        "libglintfx.so*"
        "libglintfx.a"
        # glintfx.lib: Windows/MSVC ARCHIVE artifact
        # (cmake/GlintfxInstall.cmake's install(TARGETS ... ARCHIVE
        # DESTINATION ...)) - the SAME extension names both a shared
        # build's import library and a static build's archive there,
        # so one pattern covers both; the .dll itself is a RUNTIME
        # artifact installed to CMAKE_INSTALL_BINDIR, not libdir, and
        # is out of scope for a pkg-config libdir/-L check by design.
        "glintfx.lib"
        PARENT_SCOPE
    )
endfunction()

# Reads glintfx.pc's own pkg-config VARIABLE assignments ("key=value"
# lines, in file order) directly off disk - no pkg-config binary
# involved (see this file's header, "Talking to the pkg-config BINARY
# itself"). Comment lines ("#...") and header fields ("Name:",
# "Cflags:", ...) never match this pattern: they do not start with an
# identifier immediately followed (whitespace allowed) by "=". Returns
# two PARALLEL lists (CMake has no map type): out_keys and out_values,
# RAW - not yet "${var}"-substituted; glintfx_pkgconfig_resolve_variables()
# below does that.
#
# PKG-WIN-SCOPE, adversarial review round 5 (27/08/2026) - THREE
# defects, all in the direction of REJECTING a genuinely good install,
# each MEASURED against a real pkgconf 2.5.1 on this machine
# (`PKG_CONFIG_PATH=<dir> pkgconf --variable=<key> <pkg>`), not
# reasoned about:
#   1. Whitespace around "=" ("libdir = ${prefix}/lib") is accepted by
#      real pkgconf; the previous regex required the identifier
#      immediately followed by "=", so this line matched NOTHING and
#      libdir would report undefined. Fixed by allowing "[ \t]*" on
#      both sides of "=" in the match, and never including that
#      leading/trailing whitespace in the captured value.
#   2. A trailing "#..." comment on a variable line ("libdir=${prefix}/lib
#      # note") is stripped by real pkgconf before the value is used,
#      with or without a space before "#" (measured both ways) - the
#      previous code captured everything after "=" verbatim, so the
#      comment text became part of the resolved directory and made a
#      real, populated libdir look nonexistent. Fixed by stripping
#      from the first unescaped "#" to end of line BEFORE the
#      assignment regex ever runs, the same order real pkg-config's
#      own tokenizer applies it in (a full comment line, "#..." with
#      nothing before it, already correctly matched nothing here even
#      before this fix - stripping first does not change that case).
#   3. A variable defined twice ("libdir=..." appearing on two separate
#      lines) resolves to the LAST definition in real pkgconf; the
#      previous code appended both to the list and
#      glintfx_pkgconfig_lookup_variable()'s list(FIND ...) always
#      returns the FIRST match, so a corrected later definition was
#      silently ignored in favor of a stale earlier one. Fixed by
#      removing any earlier entry for the same key before appending
#      the new one, so a key can never appear twice in out_keys and
#      the one that survives is always the one from the LAST line that
#      defined it, in its correct file-order position (this also
#      makes this function's duplicate-handling match the SAME
#      last-wins semantics glintfx_pkgconfig_read_field() below
#      already had for repeated FIELDS - before this fix, this file
#      carried two different semantics for "defined twice" depending
#      on which of its two readers looked at the line, an inconsistency
#      the adversarial reviewer named explicitly as a trap for whoever
#      edits this file next).
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_read_raw_variables pc_file out_keys out_values)
    file(STRINGS "${pc_file}" _glintfx_pc_lines)
    set(_glintfx_keys "")
    set(_glintfx_values "")
    foreach(_glintfx_pc_line IN LISTS _glintfx_pc_lines)
        string(REGEX REPLACE "#.*$" "" _glintfx_pc_line_nocomment "${_glintfx_pc_line}")
        if(_glintfx_pc_line_nocomment MATCHES "^[ \t]*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.]*)[ \t]*=[ \t]*(.*)$")
            set(_glintfx_key "${CMAKE_MATCH_1}")
            set(_glintfx_value "${CMAKE_MATCH_2}")
            string(REGEX REPLACE "[ \t]+$" "" _glintfx_value "${_glintfx_value}")
            list(FIND _glintfx_keys "${_glintfx_key}" _glintfx_dup_index)
            if(NOT _glintfx_dup_index EQUAL -1)
                list(REMOVE_AT _glintfx_keys ${_glintfx_dup_index})
                list(REMOVE_AT _glintfx_values ${_glintfx_dup_index})
            endif()
            list(APPEND _glintfx_keys "${_glintfx_key}")
            list(APPEND _glintfx_values "${_glintfx_value}")
        endif()
    endforeach()
    set(${out_keys} "${_glintfx_keys}" PARENT_SCOPE)
    set(${out_values} "${_glintfx_values}" PARENT_SCOPE)
endfunction()

# Substitutes every "${key}" reference inside `text` using the
# ALREADY-RESOLVED variables in resolved_keys/resolved_values
# (parallel lists) - one plain string replace per known variable,
# never a general expression evaluator: pkg-config's own variable
# syntax is exactly this, nothing richer.
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_substitute_text text resolved_keys resolved_values out_var)
    set(_glintfx_result "${text}")
    list(LENGTH resolved_keys _glintfx_count)
    if(_glintfx_count GREATER 0)
        math(EXPR _glintfx_last "${_glintfx_count} - 1")
        foreach(_glintfx_i RANGE 0 ${_glintfx_last})
            list(GET resolved_keys ${_glintfx_i} _glintfx_key)
            list(GET resolved_values ${_glintfx_i} _glintfx_value)
            string(REPLACE "\${${_glintfx_key}}" "${_glintfx_value}" _glintfx_result "${_glintfx_result}")
        endforeach()
    endif()
    set(${out_var} "${_glintfx_result}" PARENT_SCOPE)
endfunction()

# Resolves EVERY variable glintfx_pkgconfig_read_raw_variables() read,
# in file order, against ITSELF - pkg-config's own convention (and
# glintfx.pc.in's own layout) is that a variable's raw value may
# reference an EARLIER variable ("libdir=${exec_prefix}/lib64"), never
# a later one, so resolving left-to-right, feeding each variable's own
# resolved value forward to the ones defined after it, is enough; no
# general dependency graph is needed. seed_keys/seed_values let the
# caller pre-define a variable no "key=value" line in the file ever
# assigns - glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_on_disk() below uses
# this for "pcfiledir", pkg-config's own built-in ("the directory this
# .pc file is actually in"), which glintfx.pc.in's relocatable prefix
# ("prefix=${pcfiledir}/../..") depends on.
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_resolve_variables var_keys var_values seed_keys seed_values out_resolved_keys out_resolved_values)
    set(_glintfx_resolved_keys "${seed_keys}")
    set(_glintfx_resolved_values "${seed_values}")
    list(LENGTH var_keys _glintfx_count)
    if(_glintfx_count GREATER 0)
        math(EXPR _glintfx_last "${_glintfx_count} - 1")
        foreach(_glintfx_i RANGE 0 ${_glintfx_last})
            list(GET var_keys ${_glintfx_i} _glintfx_key)
            list(GET var_values ${_glintfx_i} _glintfx_raw_value)
            glintfx_pkgconfig_substitute_text("${_glintfx_raw_value}" "${_glintfx_resolved_keys}" "${_glintfx_resolved_values}" _glintfx_substituted)
            list(APPEND _glintfx_resolved_keys "${_glintfx_key}")
            list(APPEND _glintfx_resolved_values "${_glintfx_substituted}")
        endforeach()
    endif()
    set(${out_resolved_keys} "${_glintfx_resolved_keys}" PARENT_SCOPE)
    set(${out_resolved_values} "${_glintfx_resolved_values}" PARENT_SCOPE)
endfunction()

# Looks up ONE already-resolved variable by name. out_found is
# TRUE/FALSE, never inferred from an empty string: glintfx.pc defining
# a variable as literally empty and glintfx.pc never defining it at
# all are different defects, and glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_variable()
# below reports them with the same message on purpose (a packager
# fixing either one does the same thing: define ${var_name} properly).
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_lookup_variable resolved_keys resolved_values key out_value out_found)
    list(FIND resolved_keys "${key}" _glintfx_index)
    if(_glintfx_index EQUAL -1)
        set(${out_value} "" PARENT_SCOPE)
        set(${out_found} FALSE PARENT_SCOPE)
    else()
        list(GET resolved_values ${_glintfx_index} _glintfx_value)
        set(${out_value} "${_glintfx_value}" PARENT_SCOPE)
        set(${out_found} TRUE PARENT_SCOPE)
    endif()
endfunction()

# Reads ONE pkg-config header FIELD ("Cflags:"/"Libs:", RFC822-shaped
# "Key: value" lines, never a "key=value" variable assignment) by its
# exact name, RAW - not yet substituted. field_name is matched
# literally, anchored at both "^" and ":", so "Libs:" can never
# accidentally match a "Libs.private:" line.
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_read_field pc_file field_name out_var)
    file(STRINGS "${pc_file}" _glintfx_pc_lines)
    set(_glintfx_field_value "")
    foreach(_glintfx_pc_line IN LISTS _glintfx_pc_lines)
        if(_glintfx_pc_line MATCHES "^${field_name}:[ \t]*(.*)$")
            set(_glintfx_field_value "${CMAKE_MATCH_1}")
        endif()
    endforeach()
    set(${out_var} "${_glintfx_field_value}" PARENT_SCOPE)
endfunction()

# Validates ONE glintfx.pc variable (var_name: "includedir" or
# "libdir") against real content on disk, resolved by READING
# glintfx.pc's own text (resolved_keys/resolved_values, from
# glintfx_pkgconfig_resolve_variables() above) - no pkg-config binary
# involved. expected_content_kind is "headers" (must contain a
# glintfx/ subdirectory) or "library" (must contain one of
# glintfx_pkgconfig_library_glob_patterns()) - the only two things any
# path glintfx.pc emits ever names, same two shapes
# tests/tools/check_pkgconfig.sh's own assert_dir_contains_expected_content
# already checks in CI. FATAL_ERROR on every platform, Windows
# included, unconditionally: nothing here depends on any pkg-config
# binary's own quirks (see this file's header, "Talking to the
# pkg-config BINARY itself", for the one check that still does).
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_variable pc_file resolved_keys resolved_values var_name expected_content_kind)
    glintfx_pkgconfig_lookup_variable("${resolved_keys}" "${resolved_values}" "${var_name}" value found)
    if(NOT found OR value STREQUAL "")
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "glintfx: glintfx.pc, installed at '${pc_file}', does not "
            "define a usable '${var_name}' variable (undefined, or "
            "resolves to an empty value after substituting every "
            "'\${...}' reference this validator found in the file) - "
            "glintfx.pc should always define ${var_name}. Skip this "
            "check with GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the "
            "environment of this `cmake --install` invocation, then "
            "verify the install by hand."
        )
    endif()

    # PKG-WIN-SCOPE, adversarial review round 5 (27/08/2026) - CRITICAL,
    # reproduced live: cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH ...) with no
    # BASE_DIRECTORY resolves a relative path against
    # CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR, which in script mode (exactly how this
    # file runs, via install(CODE)/cmake -P) equals the CURRENT WORKING
    # DIRECTORY of whoever ran `cmake --install`/`cmake -P` - the
    # DISPATCH directory, attacker-controlled. MEASURED: a fixture with
    # a genuinely broken install (its compiled library artifact
    # deleted) and a relative libdir in glintfx.pc PASSED at EXIT=0
    # when this validator was invoked from a decoy directory that
    # happened to contain an unrelated file matching the same glob
    # pattern - the exact "confirmado no disco" claim this whole
    # validator exists to make, defeated by choice of CWD. The fix
    # anchors relative resolution to "pcfiledir" instead - the
    # directory glintfx.pc ITSELF physically resides in, the one
    # location pkg-config's own relocatable-prefix convention already
    # treats as ground truth (glintfx.pc.in's own "prefix=${pcfiledir}/../.."
    # depends on exactly this), and a value no packager's invocation
    # directory can influence: pc_file is this function's own absolute
    # argument, never a predicted string.
    cmake_path(GET pc_file PARENT_PATH _glintfx_content_variable_base_dir)
    cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH value BASE_DIRECTORY "${_glintfx_content_variable_base_dir}" NORMALIZE)

    if(NOT IS_DIRECTORY "${value}")
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "glintfx: glintfx.pc's ${var_name} resolves to '${value}', "
            "which does not exist on disk (installed at '${pc_file}') "
            "- the packaging step that should have created it either "
            "failed silently or put its output somewhere else. Skip "
            "this check with GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in "
            "the environment of this `cmake --install` invocation, "
            "then verify the install by hand."
        )
    endif()

    if(expected_content_kind STREQUAL "headers")
        if(NOT IS_DIRECTORY "${value}/glintfx")
            message(FATAL_ERROR
                "glintfx: glintfx.pc's ${var_name} resolves to '${value}', "
                "which exists but has no 'glintfx/' subdirectory - the "
                "installed public headers are not there (pc file: "
                "'${pc_file}'). Skip this check with "
                "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the environment "
                "of this `cmake --install` invocation, then verify the "
                "install by hand."
            )
        endif()
    elseif(expected_content_kind STREQUAL "library")
        glintfx_pkgconfig_library_glob_patterns(_glintfx_lib_pattern_names)
        set(_glintfx_lib_glob_patterns "")
        foreach(_glintfx_lib_pattern_name IN LISTS _glintfx_lib_pattern_names)
            list(APPEND _glintfx_lib_glob_patterns "${value}/${_glintfx_lib_pattern_name}")
        endforeach()
        file(GLOB _glintfx_lib_matches ${_glintfx_lib_glob_patterns})
        if(_glintfx_lib_matches STREQUAL "")
            message(FATAL_ERROR
                "glintfx: glintfx.pc's ${var_name} resolves to '${value}', "
                "which exists but has none of ${_glintfx_lib_pattern_names} - "
                "the installed library artifact is not there (pc file: "
                "'${pc_file}'). Skip this check with "
                "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the environment "
                "of this `cmake --install` invocation, then verify the "
                "install by hand."
            )
        endif()
    else()
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "glintfx: glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_variable: "
            "unknown expected_content_kind '${expected_content_kind}' "
            "(internal error in glintfx's own install(CODE) "
            "validation - this is not something a packaging layout "
            "can trigger)."
        )
    endif()
endfunction()

# Resolves EVERY -I/-L token glintfx.pc's own Cflags:/Libs: fields
# would emit for a plain (non "--static") query - the query every real
# consumer runs first - by READING and substituting the file's text
# directly (resolved_keys/resolved_values, from
# glintfx_pkgconfig_resolve_variables() above), no pkg-config binary
# involved. GODS_LAWS.md L-40 floor: a Cflags:/Libs: line with no -I/-L
# token at all would make the loops below iterate zero times and this
# function would still return without complaint - the exact "portao
# que nao olha e imprime verde" defect class L-40 exists to rule out,
# and the concrete ancestor of THIS validator (PKG-DIST's own
# output-content atom, tests/tools/check_pkgconfig.sh) was found with
# precisely this gap once already. FATAL_ERROR on every platform,
# Windows included, unconditionally.
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_flags pc_file resolved_keys resolved_values)
    # PKG-WIN-SCOPE, adversarial review round 5 (27/08/2026): same fix,
    # same reason, as glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_variable()
    # above - a relative "-I"/"-L" token must anchor to glintfx.pc's OWN
    # directory, never to the CWD of whoever invoked this validator.
    # Computed once here and reused by both the Cflags: and Libs: loops
    # below, since pc_file (and therefore its parent directory) never
    # changes within one call to this function.
    cmake_path(GET pc_file PARENT_PATH _glintfx_content_flags_base_dir)

    glintfx_pkgconfig_read_field("${pc_file}" "Cflags" _glintfx_cflags_raw)
    glintfx_pkgconfig_substitute_text("${_glintfx_cflags_raw}" "${resolved_keys}" "${resolved_values}" _glintfx_cflags_value)

    glintfx_pkgconfig_read_field("${pc_file}" "Libs" _glintfx_libs_raw)
    glintfx_pkgconfig_substitute_text("${_glintfx_libs_raw}" "${resolved_keys}" "${resolved_values}" _glintfx_libs_value)

    separate_arguments(_glintfx_cflags_tokens UNIX_COMMAND "${_glintfx_cflags_value}")
    separate_arguments(_glintfx_libs_tokens UNIX_COMMAND "${_glintfx_libs_value}")

    set(_glintfx_include_flag_count 0)
    foreach(_glintfx_token IN LISTS _glintfx_cflags_tokens)
        if(_glintfx_token MATCHES "^-I(.+)$")
            set(_glintfx_include_path "${CMAKE_MATCH_1}")
            cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH _glintfx_include_path BASE_DIRECTORY "${_glintfx_content_flags_base_dir}" NORMALIZE)
            if(NOT IS_DIRECTORY "${_glintfx_include_path}" OR NOT IS_DIRECTORY "${_glintfx_include_path}/glintfx")
                message(FATAL_ERROR
                    "glintfx: glintfx.pc's Cflags: field emitted "
                    "'${_glintfx_token}', which resolves to "
                    "'${_glintfx_include_path}' - not a directory "
                    "containing a 'glintfx/' subdirectory (pc file: "
                    "'${pc_file}'). Skip this check with "
                    "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the "
                    "environment of this `cmake --install` invocation, "
                    "then verify the install by hand."
                )
            endif()
            math(EXPR _glintfx_include_flag_count "${_glintfx_include_flag_count} + 1")
        endif()
    endforeach()

    set(_glintfx_library_flag_count 0)
    foreach(_glintfx_token IN LISTS _glintfx_libs_tokens)
        if(_glintfx_token MATCHES "^-L(.+)$")
            set(_glintfx_library_path "${CMAKE_MATCH_1}")
            cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH _glintfx_library_path BASE_DIRECTORY "${_glintfx_content_flags_base_dir}" NORMALIZE)
            glintfx_pkgconfig_library_glob_patterns(_glintfx_lib_pattern_names)
            set(_glintfx_lib_glob_patterns "")
            foreach(_glintfx_lib_pattern_name IN LISTS _glintfx_lib_pattern_names)
                list(APPEND _glintfx_lib_glob_patterns "${_glintfx_library_path}/${_glintfx_lib_pattern_name}")
            endforeach()
            file(GLOB _glintfx_lib_matches ${_glintfx_lib_glob_patterns})
            if(NOT IS_DIRECTORY "${_glintfx_library_path}" OR _glintfx_lib_matches STREQUAL "")
                message(FATAL_ERROR
                    "glintfx: glintfx.pc's Libs: field emitted "
                    "'${_glintfx_token}', which resolves to "
                    "'${_glintfx_library_path}' - not a directory "
                    "containing any of ${_glintfx_lib_pattern_names} "
                    "(pc file: '${pc_file}'). Skip this check with "
                    "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the "
                    "environment of this `cmake --install` invocation, "
                    "then verify the install by hand."
                )
            endif()
            math(EXPR _glintfx_library_flag_count "${_glintfx_library_flag_count} + 1")
        endif()
    endforeach()

    if(_glintfx_include_flag_count EQUAL 0)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "glintfx: glintfx.pc's own Cflags: field emitted ZERO -I "
            "flags (resolved: '${_glintfx_cflags_value}', pc file: "
            "'${pc_file}') - an empty Cflags: line would make this "
            "validator scan nothing and still report success "
            "(GODS_LAWS.md L-40). Skip this check with "
            "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the environment of "
            "this `cmake --install` invocation, then verify the "
            "install by hand."
        )
    endif()
    if(_glintfx_library_flag_count EQUAL 0)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "glintfx: glintfx.pc's own Libs: field emitted ZERO -L "
            "flags (resolved: '${_glintfx_libs_value}', pc file: "
            "'${pc_file}') - an empty Libs: line would make this "
            "validator scan nothing and still report success "
            "(GODS_LAWS.md L-40). Skip this check with "
            "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the environment of "
            "this `cmake --install` invocation, then verify the "
            "install by hand."
        )
    endif()

    message(STATUS
        "glintfx: post-install pkg-config content check (reading "
        "glintfx.pc directly, no pkg-config binary involved) - "
        "${_glintfx_include_flag_count} -I flag(s) and "
        "${_glintfx_library_flag_count} -L flag(s) all resolve to "
        "real, populated directories."
    )
endfunction()

# Orchestrates the WHOLE filesystem/text-only content check (LAYER A)
# against ONE installed glintfx.pc: reads its raw variables, resolves
# them (seeding "pcfiledir" with the REAL directory pc_file is
# actually in - pkg-config's own built-in, which glintfx.pc.in's
# relocatable prefix depends on: "prefix=${pcfiledir}/../.."), and
# validates includedir/libdir and every -I/-L token against real
# content on disk. Calls NO pkg-config binary at all (see this file's
# header). FATAL_ERROR on every platform, Windows included,
# unconditionally - this is the check that used to run only AFTER a
# pkg-config binary conversation had already succeeded, the exact
# ordering PKG-WIN-SCOPE's adversarial review (27/08/2026) found let a
# real broken install through on Windows, with a message claiming this
# check had already run and passed when it had never run at all.
# glintfx_validate_installed_pkgconfig() below calls this BEFORE it
# ever tries to find or talk to a pkg-config binary, on purpose.
function(glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_on_disk pc_file)
    glintfx_pkgconfig_read_raw_variables("${pc_file}" _glintfx_raw_keys _glintfx_raw_values)

    cmake_path(GET pc_file PARENT_PATH _glintfx_pcfiledir)
    set(_glintfx_seed_keys "pcfiledir")
    set(_glintfx_seed_values "${_glintfx_pcfiledir}")

    glintfx_pkgconfig_resolve_variables(
        "${_glintfx_raw_keys}" "${_glintfx_raw_values}"
        "${_glintfx_seed_keys}" "${_glintfx_seed_values}"
        _glintfx_resolved_keys _glintfx_resolved_values
    )

    glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_variable("${pc_file}" "${_glintfx_resolved_keys}" "${_glintfx_resolved_values}" includedir headers)
    glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_variable("${pc_file}" "${_glintfx_resolved_keys}" "${_glintfx_resolved_values}" libdir library)
    glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_flags("${pc_file}" "${_glintfx_resolved_keys}" "${_glintfx_resolved_values}")
endfunction()

function(glintfx_validate_installed_pkgconfig)
    if(DEFINED ENV{GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION}
       AND NOT "$ENV{GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION}" STREQUAL ""
       AND NOT "$ENV{GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION}" STREQUAL "0")
        message(STATUS
            "glintfx: post-install pkg-config validation skipped - "
            "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION is set in the "
            "environment of this `cmake --install` invocation."
        )
        return()
    endif()

    glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_resolve_staged_dir(_glintfx_pkgconfig_dir)
    set(_glintfx_pc_file "${_glintfx_pkgconfig_dir}/glintfx.pc")

    if(NOT EXISTS "${_glintfx_pc_file}")
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "glintfx: expected to find glintfx.pc at "
            "'${_glintfx_pc_file}' right after installing it, and it "
            "is not there. This usually means CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR, "
            "CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX or DESTDIR combined in a way this "
            "validation step did not anticipate. Skip this check with "
            "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the environment of "
            "this `cmake --install` invocation (or reconfigure with "
            "-DGLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=ON to disable it "
            "permanently for this build), then verify the install by "
            "hand."
        )
    endif()

    # LAYER A, unconditional, on EVERY platform, BEFORE this file ever
    # tries to find or talk to a pkg-config binary: reads glintfx.pc's
    # own text directly and confirms includedir/libdir and every -I/-L
    # token resolve to real, populated content on disk
    # (glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_on_disk(), defined above).
    # PKG-WIN-SCOPE's adversarial review (27/08/2026) found this same
    # content check used to run only AFTER the pkg-config-binary
    # `--exists` call below had already succeeded - so on Windows, one
    # single binary-conversation failure (for a reason that can have
    # nothing to do with whether the library artifact is really on
    # disk) skipped this check entirely and still reported success.
    # Calling it here, first, with FATAL_ERROR veto power that never
    # downgrades on any platform, is the fix: nothing below this line
    # can ever again claim a veto this line did not itself exercise.
    glintfx_pkgconfig_validate_content_on_disk("${_glintfx_pc_file}")

    find_program(GLINTFX_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATE_EXE NAMES pkg-config pkgconf NO_CACHE)
    if(NOT GLINTFX_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATE_EXE)
        message(WARNING
            "glintfx: pkg-config (and pkgconf) not found on PATH - "
            "skipping the pkg-config BINARY conversation "
            "('pkg-config --exists glintfx'). glintfx.pc was written "
            "to '${_glintfx_pc_file}', and its content already passed "
            "this file's own filesystem-only check (includedir, "
            "libdir, and every -I/-L token confirmed against real "
            "content on disk by reading glintfx.pc directly); there "
            "is simply no pkg-config/pkgconf on PATH to additionally "
            "confirm a REAL pkg-config binary also resolves it. "
            "Install pkg-config (or pkgconf) to get that extra "
            "confirmation, or set GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 "
            "to silence this warning intentionally."
        )
        return()
    endif()

    # PKG-VALIDATE-WINSEP, REVIVED AND FIXED BY PKG-WIN-SCOPE's revert
    # (27/08/2026): a first attempt at this (cmake_path(CONVERT ...
    # TO_NATIVE_PATH_LIST ...), reasoned but never confirmed against a
    # real Windows run) was reverted, and the whole file went Unix-only
    # for a while. The lider brought the .pc back to Windows and asked
    # for the validator to stop reprovando instalacao boa - and this
    # time there is a MEASURED answer, not a reasoned one:
    # tools/ci/diagnose-win-pkgconfig.ps1 (permanent diagnostic step,
    # `windows` job) ran a closed matrix against a live fixture on GHA
    # run 33050708122 and found that the ONLY pkg-config on that
    # windows-latest runner's PATH is Strawberry Perl's Pure-Perl
    # `PkgConfig` reimplementation (pkg-config.bat) - not a real
    # pkgconf/pkg-config binary - and that it resolves a bare
    # PKG_CONFIG_PATH value with no explicit list separator
    # ("C:/Users/.../pkgconfig") by falling back to POSIX-style
    # splitting on ':', which shreds the drive letter itself into a
    # bogus one-letter search directory ("C", "/Users/.../pkgconfig")
    # - exactly the failure this file's PREVIOUS attempt was reasoning
    # about, confirmed for real this time. The SAME value with an
    # explicit trailing ';' (semicolon) resolved correctly in every
    # cell of that matrix, forward slash or backslash: the presence of
    # ';' makes it split on the Windows-native separator instead of
    # falling back to ':'. cmake_path(CONVERT ... TO_NATIVE_PATH_LIST
    # ...) alone does not guarantee that trailing separator for a
    # SINGLE-entry list (there is nothing else in the list to separate
    # from), which is almost certainly why the earlier, reasoned-only
    # attempt still failed on real Windows CI (GHA run for commit
    # 9a863c7, job "Windows - compartilhado": 'pkg-config --exists'
    # failed against a glintfx.pc this file's own resolver had just
    # proven existed, PKG_CONFIG_PATH shown with forward slashes, no
    # separator). The fix below is therefore explicit, not left to
    # cmake_path alone: on WIN32, convert to native slashes AND append
    # a literal trailing native list separator, so the value ALWAYS
    # contains at least one, regardless of list length.
    #
    # PROVEN on POSIX (this machine, unchanged from before): for a
    # plain path, a path with a doubled '//' separator, and a path
    # with a trailing '/', cmake_path(CONVERT ... TO_NATIVE_PATH_LIST
    # ...) is byte-identical to the untouched original - nothing
    # observable changes here on Linux, Fedora, Ubuntu, Arch or
    # CachyOS, and the WIN32 branch below never runs there at all.
    #
    # NOT proven, and not claimed: that every pkg-config a real
    # packager might have on PATH on some OTHER Windows machine (a
    # genuine MSYS2 pkgconf, a vcpkg-shipped one, anything else
    # GODS_LAWS.md LEI ZERO's public-and-unknown consumer base could
    # combine with Windows) parses PKG_CONFIG_PATH the same way
    # Strawberry Perl's emulator does. That is exactly why the
    # `--exists` check right below downgrades to a WARNING instead of
    # a FATAL_ERROR on WIN32 if it still fails after this fix - see
    # this file's header, "Talking to the pkg-config BINARY itself".
    if(WIN32)
        cmake_path(CONVERT "${_glintfx_pkgconfig_dir}" TO_NATIVE_PATH_LIST _glintfx_pkgconfig_path_native)
        string(APPEND _glintfx_pkgconfig_path_native ";")
        set(ENV{PKG_CONFIG_PATH} "${_glintfx_pkgconfig_path_native}")
    else()
        set(ENV{PKG_CONFIG_PATH} "${_glintfx_pkgconfig_dir}")
    endif()

    execute_process(
        COMMAND "${GLINTFX_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATE_EXE}" --print-errors --exists glintfx
        RESULT_VARIABLE _glintfx_exists_result
        ERROR_VARIABLE _glintfx_exists_error
        OUTPUT_QUIET
    )
    if(NOT _glintfx_exists_result EQUAL 0)
        if(WIN32)
            # The LAYER A content check above (glintfx_pkgconfig_
            # validate_content_on_disk()) has ALREADY run, unconditionally,
            # by the time this line can even be reached, and it is what
            # actually confirmed glintfx.pc, the headers and the library
            # artifact are genuinely on disk with real content - not this
            # `--exists` call, and not any other check below it. What
            # could NOT be confirmed is whether THIS pkg-config binary, on
            # THIS machine, can also find and parse glintfx.pc via
            # PKG_CONFIG_PATH - a binary-specific quirk this file cannot
            # enumerate for every Windows pkg-config that could exist
            # (GODS_LAWS.md L-27: declared downgrade, not a silent "ok").
            # The message below names exactly what was and was not
            # verified, and by which check, never a generic pass.
            message(WARNING
                "glintfx: post-install pkg-config CONVERSATION could not "
                "be verified on this Windows machine - 'pkg-config "
                "--exists glintfx' failed against the file just "
                "installed at '${_glintfx_pc_file}' "
                "(PKG_CONFIG_PATH=$ENV{PKG_CONFIG_PATH}): "
                "${_glintfx_exists_error}. This file's OWN "
                "filesystem-only content check already ran before this "
                "point (reading glintfx.pc directly, no pkg-config "
                "binary involved) and already confirmed glintfx.pc, the "
                "headers and the library artifact are genuinely on disk "
                "with real content; only whether THIS machine's "
                "pkg-config binary additionally resolves them via "
                "PKG_CONFIG_PATH is unverified. Set "
                "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 to silence this "
                "warning intentionally, or verify by hand with the "
                "pkg-config on this machine."
            )
            return()
        endif()
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "glintfx: 'pkg-config --exists glintfx' failed against "
            "the file just installed at '${_glintfx_pc_file}' "
            "(PKG_CONFIG_PATH=${_glintfx_pkgconfig_dir}): "
            "${_glintfx_exists_error}. Skip this check with "
            "GLINTFX_SKIP_PKGCONFIG_VALIDATION=1 in the environment of "
            "this `cmake --install` invocation, then verify the "
            "install by hand."
        )
    endif()

    message(STATUS
        "glintfx: post-install pkg-config validation passed - "
        "glintfx.pc at '${_glintfx_pc_file}' passed this file's own "
        "filesystem-only content check, and a real pkg-config binary "
        "on this machine's PATH also finds it via PKG_CONFIG_PATH."
    )
endfunction()

glintfx_validate_installed_pkgconfig()
